    "README.md": "# STM32 board\n\nSTM32F103C8T6 with 8 MHz crystal, SWD header, USB-C and 3.3 V LDO.\n\nStarted from the Jumper **STM32 board** template. Symbols and footprints come from the KiCad 9 libraries.\n\n## What is here\n\n- `stm32.kicad_sch`: schematic. Pins are tied together with net labels and power symbols.\n- `stm32.kicad_pcb`: board with the outline and every footprint placed and netted, not routed yet.\n- `.jumper.yml`: checks. Unrouted connections are not counted as errors until you switch `fail_on_unconnected` on.\n\n## Next steps\n\n1. Check every value and footprint against the parts you will buy.\n2. Arrange the parts on the board and route it.\n3. Set `fail_on_unconnected: true` in `.jumper.yml` so unrouted connections fail the check.\n"
